        exam: [.direct("What did the bank statements show?", "\"Overlapping deposits across three banks, with checks drawn on empty accounts. The pattern built a $60,000 float that collapsed.\""), .direct("What does the transfer log show?", "\"Daily transfers moving money between the accounts. The first check was written about six months before the float collapsed.\""), .direct("What do the check images show?", "\"Checks drawn on accounts that had no money. {D} was covering one with another, buying time with each one.\""), .direct("When did you first notice a problem?", "\"The bank detected overlapping deposits from two other banks in the same days. We pulled statements and saw checks being written against accounts that did not have the money.\""), .direct("How did the float grow?", "\"Each day a check from one bank covered a check written at another, and the amounts crept up. By month six the exposure totaled $60,000.\""), .direct("What happened when the float collapsed?", "\"Deposits were returned unpaid at all three banks on the same morning. The balances went negative, and the banks froze the accounts.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} misunderstood posting times, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A person can be confused about when a check posts. But daily transfers for months suggest a method.\""), .cross("Did {DL} take money out for personal use?", "\"I can't point to a specific personal purchase. I focused on the float itself. I can say the float collapsed.\""), .cross("Was {DL} warned by the banks?", "\"The banks were notified when it fell apart. I can't say precisely who warned {D.him} and when.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever repay any of the money?", "\"I know of a $20,000 repayment. I do not have more detail on how it was funded.\""), .cross("Was this the defendant's own personal account or a business account?", "\"Mostly a business account. We have no sign the funds went to anything but the business.\"")],
